             GIS Layers        
    
	  	  

	   

	   

			 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Geographic information Systems (GIS) play a vital role in helping municipalities manage infrastructure, services, and growth. By mapping and analyzing spatial data, city planners and local governments can make informed decisions on land use, zoning, transportation, utilities, and emergency response.  GIS is used to monitor road conditions, track public assets (like streetlights and water lines), assess environmental impact, and plan new developments. It also enhances public safety through real-time mapping during natural disasters, improves waste collection routing, and supports citizen engagement through interactive city maps.  
     

 
